menuconfig HCP_SWITCH
	bool "HCP relay switch control (K1/K2)"
	default y
	depends on GPIO

if HCP_SWITCH

config HCP_ENABLE_SWITCH_CONTROL
	bool "Compile relay control into the application logic"
	default y
	help
	  Speaks the "<sn>-K" contract with Home Assistant: accepts
	  <sn>-K/control/cmd, drives hcp-k1/hcp-k2, keeps their state across a reboot
	  and reports it on <sn>-K/notify, and announces the device with its
	  switch_count on every connect. This is the shape of the previous firmware's
	  CONFIG_ENABLE_SWITCH_CONTROL path (main/solar_manager.cpp:108-122 plus
	  components/switch_ctrl), which is what the integration in the field expects.

	  Off on a board whose relays are not wired: the relay outputs are real pins on
	  every Helios board, so turning this off is a statement about a build, not
	  about hardware.

endif
